* Calculate energy and run simulations with FACTS implicit solvation model  (param22)
* Reference:
* Haberthuer and Caflisch, J. Comput. Chem., 29(5): 701-715, 2008
* DOI: 10.1002/jcc.20832
*

! based on step2_implicit.inp, modified by SB May 2019 for simple analyses
! this is the 'explicit loop' example
! (see https://www.charmm.org/charmm/documentation/by-version/c42b1/params/doc/correl/)

!DIMENS CHSIZE 3000000 MAXRES 3000000

! Read topology and parameter files
stream toppar.str

! Read PSF
open read unit 10 card name step1_pdbreader.psf
read psf  unit 10 card xplor

! Read COOR
open read unit 10 card name step1_pdbreader.crd
read coor unit 10 card

! example of analysis looping explicitly over trajectory
!    we compute: secondary structure assignment
!                (optionally) SASA

open read unit 13 file name prod.1.dcd
open writ unit 20 form name ana2.dat

traj query unit 13 ! get info from trajectory
                   ! we are curious about ?nfile = number of frames in traj.
calc nframes = ?nfile
! In general, nframes = number of trajectories times ?nfile

! for rmsd need ref. coors in comp set
coor copy comp

! some quantities cannot be computed by correl; however,
! trajetories can be read frame by frame from a CHARMM loop, and 
! then the whole suite of COOR, IC etc. commands is at your
! disposal. This is, however, not very fast ..

traj iread 13 nread 1 ! first unit number for trajectory, number of trajectories
set fram 1

define prot sele segi pro* end
! calculate secondary structure
coor secs sele prot end sele prot end comp

echu 20

label loop

  traj read ! read frame from trajetory
  coor secs sele prot end sele prot end quiet ! sec. structure
  !! uncomment to compute SASA (this is expensive, so might require use of SKIP ..)
  !! coor surf sele prot end rprobe 1.6 accuracy 0.05 acce ! solvent accessible surface

  !! if you want SASA calc. as well, comment next line and uncomment the 2nd echo line ..
  echo @fram ?nalpha ?nbeta ! write to output file 
  !! echo @fram ?nalpha ?nbeta ?area ! write to output file

! check whether we are done
incr fram by 1
if fram le @nframes goto loop

stop
